 "recognition_note": "The antigen was identified as human IL6ST/gp130. A 2024 paper shows a 4.40-A gp130–B-S12 Fab reconstruction and historical sources map B-S12 regionally, but no dated source links the supplied VH/VL sequences to B-S12, A5, or G7. I therefore did not identify the supplied antibody or promote B-S12 evidence to Tier A.",
 "what_separated_them": "No candidate had confirmed Tier A evidence about the supplied binder. The order is conditional on dated B-S12 evidence placing a non-sequence-identified Fab regionally at membrane-distal D2/D2-D3, independent geometry favoring compact exposed footprints, and overlap analysis showing that C1/C3/C4 are competing drawings of one broad region rather than independent confirmations. C1 narrowly wins compactness and regional placement; C3/C4 retain substantial mass. Tier B chemistry mainly keeps C4/C8 live and filters C2 rather than localizing by itself.",
